 L89). Plan one slider per part group from the start (e.g. Jacket, Pants, Top, Bottom, Armour full / limbs only / off),
 each owning disjoint objects; step 0 = the default look and the last step = off (strip-safe for CustomizeAll(99)); eve
ry blend-shape key has exactly one owner slot (decompose union keys, list conjunction approximations); visibility that
depends on two slots uses m_IsActive from one slot and the renderer's m_Enabled from the other; solve or re-key the cli
p fix per (garment x armour state), hold the armour-fit body keys per armour step, and gate every reference figure in g
ame on a real build. 00a L93-L96 documents this as a retrofit, but the playbook still plans an outfit-preset slider. Se
cond pass (gap study): shipped reference design - each garment has its own 2-3 step slider, a step changes at most 8 ob
jects, 136 of 143 characters have no duplicate step and the 5 references have no unreachable renderer. Gate from the Cu
stomize clips: a renderer is reachable if some frame (or the prefab default when unkeyed) has both m_IsActive and m_Ena
bled on; count the objects changed per step and the identical steps; list GameObjects keyed by several clips and give e
ach one owning clip (the docs disagree on how several clips combine: 19 l.417 says the game ANDs m_IsActive over clips,
 37 l.148 counts OR for cost bounds, the gap study saw the last sampled clip win; settle it with one in-game test). The
 playbook part 2 item 2 (l.736) keeps duplicate steps on purpose so saved slider indices stay valid: report identical s
teps and allow only those. The Clothes panel was observed to list Customize sliders in reverse order of the Animation c
omponent's clip list, so order the list so the main sliders show first (confirm with REA on the panel builder); keep sl
iders at <= 4-8 steps with a step legend in the README and 'off' last; gate that every reference-sheet look is reachabl
e with slider settings and that all sliders at max give nude + hair.
